## Branding and teams

On the hosted service: a shared workspace with roles and SSO, and secret links sent from a domain your recipients already trust.

- **[Custom domains](/en/custom-domains/)** — DNS validation, branding, and an incoming page for secrets sent to you.
- **[Organizations](/en/organizations/)** — invite members, assign roles, and review the audit trail.
- **[Single sign-on](/en/organizations/sso/)** — Entra, OIDC and SAML sign-in for your organization.

## Development

Create and retrieve secrets from scripts, CI pipelines and your own applications.

- **[REST API](/en/api/)** — regional endpoints, authentication, and the full reference at api.onetimesecret.com.
- **[Client libraries](/en/api/client-libraries/)** — official and community SDKs, and which ones support regions and custom domains.

## Self-hosting

Run the same open-source application that powers onetimesecret.com on your own infrastructure.

- **[Hosted or self-hosted?](/en/start/hosted-or-self-hosted/)** — what changes when you run the servers, and what doesn't.
- **[Installation](/en/install/docker/)** — Docker, Linux, reverse proxy and TLS, running as a service.
- **[Configuration and upgrades](/en/self-hosting/)** — configuration, environment variables, and version upgrade guides.

## How the service handles your data

For security reviews, procurement, and anyone deciding whether to trust us with a secret.

- **Secret content is destroyed on view or at expiry.** Every secret has a lifetime. Receipts and audit records have separate retention periods. [Data protection](/en/security/data-protection/)
- **Encrypted in transit and at rest**, on every plan. An optional passphrase is required to reveal a protected secret. [Best practices](/en/security/best-practices/)
- **You choose the region.** Data is processed and stored in the EU, UK, US, Canada or New Zealand. [Where your data lives](/en/security/where-your-data-lives/)
- **No trackers, no analytics, no marketing email.** We store only what the service needs to run. [Our principles](/en/security/our-principles/)
- **Open source.** Read the code, or run it on your own infrastructure. [GitHub](https://github.com/onetimesecret/onetimesecret)

Found a security issue? [Report it here](/en/security/vulnerability-disclosure/).

Opened a link someone sent you? See [what recipients see](/en/share/what-recipients-see/) and [what to do when a link doesn't work](/en/share/when-a-link-doesnt-work/). New to the service? Begin with [Getting started](/en/start/).
